(645,1337,'Inflammation of the duodenum (first part of small intestine).','en',2,'2026-06-24 11:41:56',NULL,NULL,'12982FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(646,1338,'Disorders of speech articulation caused by imperfect coordination of pharnyx, larnyx, tongue, or face muscles. This may result from CRANIAL NERVE DISEASES; NEUROMUSCULAR DISEASES; CEREBELLAR DISEASES; BASAL GANGLIA DISEASES; BRAIN STEM diseases; or diseases of the corticobulbar tracts (see PYRAMIDAL TRACTS). The cortical language centers are intact in this condition. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p489)','en',2,'2026-06-24 11:41:56',NULL,NULL,'12978FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
