(844,1733,'DEF: Malaria in pregnant woman defore delivery. DESC: Malaria in pregnancy increases the risk of maternal anaemia, stillbirth, spontaneous abortion, low birth weight and neonatal death. WHO recommends a package of interventions for the prevention and control of malaria during pregnancy:\r\n\r\nUse of insecticide treated nets (ITNs) to prevent infection \r\nIntermittent Preventive Treatment (IPT) to prevent asymptomatic infections among pregnant women living in areas of moderate or high transmission of P. falciparum \r\nEffective case management for malaria illness and anaemia. \r\n \r\nREF: WHO','en',2,'2026-06-24 11:42:05',NULL,NULL,'10420FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
