(1252,2662,'State in which an individual perceives or experiences a sensation of unreality concerning the self or the environment; it is seen in disorders such as schizophrenia, affection disorders, organic mental disorders, and personality disorders. (APA, Thesaurus of Psychological Index Terms, 8th ed.)','en',2,'2026-06-24 11:42:26',NULL,NULL,'5528FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1253,2664,'Organic mental disorders in which there is impairment of the ability to maintain awareness of self and environment and to respond to environmental stimuli. Dysfunction of the cerebral hemispheres or brain stem RETICULAR FORMATION may result in this condition.','en',2,'2026-06-24 11:42:26',NULL,NULL,'5524FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1254,2665,'Psychotic organic mental disorders resulting from the toxic effect of drugs and chemicals or other harmful substance.','en',2,'2026-06-24 11:42:26',NULL,NULL,'5513FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1255,2668,'Difficulty in swallowing.','en',2,'2026-06-24 11:42:26',NULL,NULL,'5495FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1256,2670,'Chronically depressed mood that occurs for most of the day more days than not for at least 2 years. The required minimum duration in children to make this diagnosis is 1 year. During periods of depressed mood, at least 2 of the following additional symptoms are present: poor appetite or overeating, insomnia or hypersomnia, low energy or fatigue, low self esteem, poor concentration or difficulty making decisions, and feelings of hopelessness. (DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-06-24 11:42:26',NULL,NULL,'5488FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
